course: dictionary
lesson: 2366
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Cuisine is one of them. Its first meaning is a style of cooking from a certain country or region, like Italian cuisine.
explain: Its second meaning is the food served, especially good-quality food. When someone says «the restaurant's cuisine», they mean the food that restaurant serves.
explain: French words can look like English words but mean something else. In «Voici la cuisine, à côté il y a le salon», cuisine means kitchen, because the sentence is about rooms in a house.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Ask: is this about a country's style of cooking, the food served, or a room? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Cuisine means a style of cooking from a certain country or region.
fact: «French cuisine» is famous for sauces and pastries.
fact: «Japanese cuisine» is famous for sushi.
fact: Cuisine can also mean the food served, especially good-quality food.
fact: In French, «la cuisine» means the kitchen and also the cooking, which is why English says «French cuisine».
exercise: «French cuisine is famous for sauces and pastries.» What does cuisine mean here? | A type of sports shoe | A room in a house | *A style of cooking from a certain country | A small, quiet bird
exercise: «The restaurant's cuisine was excellent, with fresh fish and rich sauces.» What does cuisine mean here? | Only the kitchen where the cooks work | A tourist guide book | *The food served, especially good-quality food | A map of the country
exercise: «Voici la cuisine, à côté il y a le salon.» In this French sentence, what does la cuisine mean? | *Kitchen | Bedroom | Living room | Cooking lessons
test: Which cuisine is famous for sushi? | Indian | French | Italian | *Japanese
test: Why does English say «French cuisine»? | *Because la cuisine in French means both the kitchen and the cooking | Because cuisine means a map | Because cuisine is a French word for music | Because French people only eat pastries
exam: Ella reads «The cuisine of the region uses lots of olive oil and fresh herbs.» Which meaning fits best? | A type of tent | Kitchen | A cold drink | *A style of cooking from that region
